CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
must never appear
--
N5008 [temp.inst]/11: a non-virtual member operator of a class template shall
not be implicitly instantiated unless odr-used.  Under lazy on-odr-use
instantiation the unused operator+ is never instantiated, so its assertion
"must never appear" does not enter the goto program and the forbidden pattern
must be absent.

This became CORE once non-virtual operators were deferred together with
ordinary member functions.  See
doc/architectural/cpp-extern-template-member-instantiation.md §13.
